  "steps": [
    "Boil 3 tomatoes and blend them in a mixer.",
    "In a pan, add 1 tsp olive oil and add tha garlic. Sauté until golden brown and then add onion. Sauté for another 2 mins.",
    "Then add the boiled tomatoes paste. Cover and let it cook for 4-5 mins.",
    "Add a dash of water to adjust consistency and then add ketchup and seasonings.",
    "Cook for 3-4 mins and add fresh basil.",
    "Now turn off the gas, let it cool down for 10 mins and using a hand blender, blend this sauce well. Don’t make it too fine. Just make sure its well combined and gets that pizza sauce like coarse consistency.",
    "Protip: Let the sauce rest for 2 hrs before you use it on the pizza base for the flavors to really rise.",
    "Assemble your pizza and bake in oven/airfryer for 10-15 mins at 200 degrees. Please keep checking in the mid so it doesn’t burn."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Sweeten the sauce with sugar or stevia; use parmesan or mozzarella on top.",
